		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"### Legend<br><br>Cyan: curriculum hierarchy (module guide to lesson).<br>Blue: lesson to atomic topic.<br>Green: topic grounds in a source record.<br>Orange: uncertainty and limits.<br>Purple: hypotheses and open questions.<br><br>An edge records a relationship in this library; it is never a causal claim.","x":1260,"y":-343,"width":520,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","text":"### Uncertainty<br><br>- Concentration is a proxy for exposure<br>- Dropout undercounts side effects<br>- Mechanism knowledge is not clinical evidence","x":-488,"y":1290,"width":500,"height":330,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","text":"### Open questions<br><br>- How much variability in exposure comes from adherence versus metabolism?<br>- How do downstream adaptations change a drug's effect over time?<br>- What determines an individual's time to steady state beyond half-life?","x":-412,"y":1660,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"6"},
